qs.append({"q":"Which leaders are identified as the most prominent representatives of the militant nationalist school of thought in Bengal, Maharashtra and Punjab respectively?","o":["Aurobindo Ghosh/Bipin Chandra Pal (Bengal), Bal Gangadhar Tilak (Maharashtra), Lala Lajpat Rai (Punjab)","Surendranath Banerjea (Bengal), Pherozshah Mehta (Maharashtra), Dadabhai Naoroji (Punjab)","Ashwini Kumar Datta (Bengal), M.G. Ranade (Maharashtra), Syed Ahmed Khan (Punjab)","Debendranath Tagore (Bengal), Jyotiba Phule (Maharashtra), Dayananda Saraswati (Punjab)"],"a":0,"e":"Aurobindo Ghosh and Bipin Chandra Pal in Bengal, Tilak in Maharashtra, and Lala Lajpat Rai in Punjab were leading figures of militant nationalism, together known as 'Lal-Bal-Pal' alongside Aurobindo."})

