qs.append({"q":"Which of the following is identified as one of the three key reasons for the Extremists gaining dominant influence over the Swadeshi Movement in Bengal after 1905?","o":["The Moderate-led movement had failed to yield results, and government repression had embittered the nationalists","The Moderates voluntarily handed over leadership to the Extremists","The British government officially endorsed Extremist leadership","The Muslim League fully supported the Extremist programme"],"a":0,"e":"Among the reasons cited were the failure of Moderate methods to achieve results, divisive government tactics, and severe government repression, all of which embittered nationalists and strengthened Extremist influence."})

