qs.append({"q":"Which of the following is identified as a negative or 'socially reactionary' aspect of the Extremist ideology despite its politically progressive stance on mass mobilisation?","o":["Revivalist and obscurantist undertones, such as Tilak's opposition to the Age of Consent Bill and use of Hindu festivals, which alienated many Muslims","Complete rejection of any religious symbolism in politics","Full support for women's rights and gender equality reforms","Active collaboration with the British government on all policy matters"],"a":0,"e":"The Extremists' association with Hindu symbols and festivals, and figures like Tilak opposing certain social reforms, gave their movement revivalist and communal undertones that alienated Muslims."})

